       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 16,000 mg/day of ibuprofen has no therapeutic use. It is in the range where serious toxicity is expected, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis. Normal kidney and liver function won't prevent that. A higher dose also doesn't give more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, because ibuprofen's benefit plateaus well below this.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO QID (3,200 mg/day, the maximum labeled dose)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO QID, or another dose you choose within the labeled range\n- A multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen. Tell me the indication and I can enter the components you pick.\n\nIf there is a specific clinical reason for a dose this high, I suggest discussing it with pharmacy or toxicology first. An order that exceeds the maximum would also normally need a pharmacist override."
      }
